{%- comment -%}
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ELIGIBLE PROMOTIONS (custom vcollect)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Lists the promotions that are running AND that cover the product being viewed.

Liquid cannot read Shopify discounts: the storefront exposes no `discounts` object, and the Storefront API does not
expose them either. The discount stays the source of truth; migrations/sync-promotions.mjs copies the ones flagged
`vcollect.afficher_sur_fiche` into `vcollect_promotion` metaobject entries, which Liquid can read.

The dates are compared here, at render time, so a promotion appears and drops off on its own at the hour it starts and
ends. Nothing to push, no script to re-run, and no cache to wait for.

********************************************
The panel
********************************************

A solid panel in the logo blue with white type, on merchant request: the offer has to be the thing you cannot miss in
the product column. It sits inside the tinted `custom_info_wrapper` panel, so it carries only its fill, no border and
no shadow, and one flat colour with no gradient.

Three lines, each carrying information rather than decoration:

  1. What the offer is, and how long is left. The deadline is the store's own <countdown-timer>, the element the home
     page banner already runs on, so the urgency is real and ticking rather than a static "hurry" label.
  2. What this product costs under the offer, against what it costs without it.
  3. The code, framed and centred at the foot of the panel. It is the only part meant to be acted on rather than
     read, hence the only outline and the only centred block, and the button copies the code in one tap, which is
     what saves a mobile shopper from typing it wrong.

********************************************
The discounted price
********************************************

Measured against a real cart on 08/08/2026, discount code VCOLLECT10: on a 0,99 € subtotal Shopify takes 0,09 € and
not 0,10 €, and on 2,97 € it takes 0,29 € and not 0,30 €. Shopify truncates to the cent below, it does not round.
Liquid's integer `divided_by` truncates the same way, so `price | times: percent | divided_by: 100` reproduces
Shopify's own arithmetic to the cent. Do not "fix" this into a rounding, it would overstate the discount.

The price is only printed for a percentage with no minimum purchase (`prix_barre`, decided by the sync script): under a
minimum, the price shown would be one the shopper may well not get.

********************************************
Supported variables
********************************************

* product: the product whose eligibility is tested
* form_id: the product form id, so the price follows the selected variant
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  A sold-out product cannot be bought, so a discount on it is noise at best and a tease at worst. `product.available`
  is false only when NO variant is buyable, so a product with one sold-out size keeps its promotion.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if product.available -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign now_timestamp = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0
    assign price_already_shown = false
  -%}

  {%- capture promotions_markup -%}
    {%- for promotion in metaobjects.vcollect_promotion.values -%}
      {%- liquid
        unless promotion.afficher_sur_fiche.value
          continue
        endunless

        comment
          A blank start means "already running", the same way a blank end means "no end date": an empty field must
          never hide a promotion the merchant deliberately flagged.
        endcomment
        assign starts_at = promotion.date_debut.value | date: '%s' | plus: 0
        if starts_at > now_timestamp
          continue
        endif

        assign ends_at = promotion.date_fin.value | date: '%s' | plus: 0
        if ends_at > 0 and ends_at <= now_timestamp
          continue
        endif

        assign is_eligible = false

        case promotion.portee.value
          when 'collections'
            for promotion_collection in promotion.collections.value
              for product_collection in product.collections
                if product_collection.id == promotion_collection.id
                  assign is_eligible = true
                  break
                endif
              endfor

              if is_eligible
                break
              endif
            endfor
          when 'produits'
            for promotion_product in promotion.produits.value
              if promotion_product.id == product.id
                assign is_eligible = true
                break
              endif
            endfor
          else
            assign is_eligible = true
        endcase

        unless is_eligible
          continue
        endunless

        comment
          Only the first promotion prices the product. Two struck prices would each ignore the other, and nothing
          guarantees two discounts combine, so the second one would be a promise the cart does not keep.
        endcomment
        assign show_price = false
        if promotion.prix_barre.value and promotion.pourcentage.value > 0 and price_already_shown == false
          assign show_price = true
          assign price_already_shown = true
        endif
      -%}

      <div class="promotion-offer">
        <div class="promotion-offer__top">
          <span class="promotion-offer__label">{{ promotion.titre.value | escape }}</span>

          {%- if ends_at > 0 -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              Server-rendered first, then kept ticking by custom-countdown.js. A shopper who never receives the script
              still reads how long is left instead of a row of zeros.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign remaining = ends_at | minus: now_timestamp
              assign remaining_days = remaining | divided_by: 86400
              assign remaining_hours = remaining | modulo: 86400 | divided_by: 3600
              assign remaining_minutes = remaining | modulo: 3600 | divided_by: 60
            -%}

            <countdown-timer class="promotion-offer__countdown" target="{{ promotion.date_fin.value | date: '%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S%z' }}">
              <span><b data-countdown-days>{{ remaining_days }}</b>{{ 'product.promotions.unit_days' | t }}</span>
              <span><b data-countdown-hours>{{ remaining_hours }}</b>{{ 'product.promotions.unit_hours' | t }}</span>
              <span><b data-countdown-minutes>{{ remaining_minutes }}</b>{{ 'product.promotions.unit_minutes' | t }}</span>
            </countdown-timer>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        {%- if show_price -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            <variant-inventory> is the theme's own element: it hides every direct child whose data-variant-id is not
            the selected one, so the price follows the variant picker without a line of JavaScript here.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <variant-inventory {% if form_id %}form="{{ form_id }}"{% endif %} class="promotion-offer__prices">
            {%- for variant in product.variants -%}
              {%- unless variant.available -%}
                {%- continue -%}
              {%- endunless -%}

              {%- liquid
                assign discount_amount = variant.price | times: promotion.pourcentage.value | divided_by: 100
                assign discounted_price = variant.price | minus: discount_amount
              -%}

              <span data-variant-id="{{ variant.id }}" {% unless variant == product.selected_or_first_available_variant %}hidden{% endunless %}>
                <span class="promotion-offer__price">{{ discounted_price | money }}</span>
                <s class="promotion-offer__was">{{ variant.price | money }}</s>
              </span>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </variant-inventory>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if promotion.message.value != blank -%}
          <p class="promotion-offer__note">{{ promotion.message.value | escape }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if promotion.code.value != blank -%}
          <div class="promotion-offer__code">
            <span class="promotion-offer__code-hint">{{ 'product.promotions.code_hint' | t }}</span>

            <copy-code class="promotion-offer__coupon" code="{{ promotion.code.value | escape }}">
              <button type="button" class="promotion-offer__coupon-button">
                <span class="promotion-offer__coupon-code">{{ promotion.code.value | escape }}</span>
                <span
                  class="promotion-offer__coupon-action"
                  data-copy-label
                  data-copied-label="{{ 'product.promotions.copied' | t | escape }}"
                  aria-live="polite"
                >
                  {{- 'product.promotions.copy' | t -}}
                </span>
              </button>
            </copy-code>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}

  {%- if promotions_markup != blank -%}
    <script type="module" src="{{ 'custom-countdown.js' | asset_url }}"></script>
    <script type="module" src="{{ 'custom-copy-code.js' | asset_url }}"></script>

    <div class="promotion-offer-list" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
      {{- promotions_markup -}}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
